    <bpmn:process id="W_W2523" name="W2523. Disaster Recovery Financial Impact Reporting &amp; Budget Rebalancing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Post-disaster financial impact exceeds PHP 10M or affects &gt;10 stores
Frequency: 2–4 significant events per year
Volume: 1 financial impact report per event
Owner: FP&amp;A Manager
Participants: FP&amp;A Mgr, Finance, Treasury, Insurance, COO, CFO
Source: workflow W2523 — Disaster Recovery Financial Impact Reporting &amp; Budget Rebalancing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W2523_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W2523_Lane1" name="FP&amp;A Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W2523_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W2523_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W2523_Lane2" name="CFO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W2523_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W2523_Lane3" name="Treasury Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W2523_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W2523_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W2523_Start5" name="Post-disaster financial impact exceeds PHP 10M or affects &gt;10 stores">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W2523_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W2523_Task6" name="FP&amp;A compiles disaster financial impact: revenue loss (closed days × daily…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: FP&amp;A compiles disaster financial impact: revenue loss (closed days × daily revenue per store), inventory write-offs, facility repair costs, emergency procurement premiums, employee assistance costs, donation costs, insurance recoveries
Responsible (R): FP&amp;A Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 3–5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W2523_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W2523_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W2523_Task7" name="CFO reviews impact vs. insurance coverage and retained risk; updates annual P&amp;L…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: CFO reviews impact vs. insurance coverage and retained risk; updates annual P&amp;L forecast; proposes budget reallocation if net impact &gt; PHP 50M (defer non-critical capex, adjust marketing spend, reduce discretionary expenses)
Responsible (R): CFO
Accountable (A): CEO / Board
Duration: 1–2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W2523_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W2523_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W2523_Task8" name="Treasury manages cash flow impact: coordinates with insurance for advance…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Treasury manages cash flow impact: coordinates with insurance for advance payments, accelerates AR collections in unaffected regions, manages vendor payment prioritization, adjusts capital expenditure timing
Responsible (R): Treasury Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W2523_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W2523_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W2523_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W2523_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W2523_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-438 (ensure controlled execution — Post-Disaster Recovery &amp; Community Support (PA-69.3).) | - operational: FP&amp;A Manager review and approval gate
Owner: FP&amp;A Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
